WEBVTT

00:09:28.213 --> 00:09:30.232
And that was important
and necessary to do.

00:09:30.256 --> 00:09:32.593
We couldn't have had
the Silicon Valley revolution

00:09:32.617 --> 00:09:35.635
unless we had an individual culture
of rebellion and creativity.

00:09:35.659 --> 00:09:37.247
But we've had 60 years of it now,

00:09:37.271 --> 00:09:39.306
and we've sort of run out the string.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:43.055
And we've created a culture where we think
of ourselves as buffered individuals

00:09:43.079 --> 00:09:46.401
who create our own sense of meaning,
our own sense of purpose in life,

00:09:46.425 --> 00:09:48.619
and we've destroyed
the connections between us.

00:09:48.643 --> 00:09:50.748
And that, to me,
is the heart of the problem.

00:09:50.772 --> 00:09:53.497
CA: Is it possible that
the generation in the '60s,

00:09:53.521 --> 00:09:57.476
the hippies and fellow
travelers, were successful?

00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:00.025
Because they had grown up
in a different situation.